# SteadyDose environment configuration (example).
# These are only needed when you want cloud sync (auth + multi-device).
# Stages 0–2 / 6 / 7 run fully offline with no env required.
#
# For LOCAL dev you don't fill this in by hand: run `supabase start`, then copy
# the printed "API URL" and "anon key" into .env.local (or run `pnpm local:env`).
# For a real deploy, read them from your Supabase project's API settings.
# The anon key is publishable (RLS protects data); NEVER ship the service-role key.
# Only this example file is tracked — never commit .env.local.

# Supabase (cloud sync)
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
